---
/**
 * Privacy page. Not boilerplate filler: ValidSim's product handles API keys, so
 * an enterprise buyer will ask what it stores and what it logs. Answering
 * precisely is a sales asset.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site } from '../data/content';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — ValidSim"
  description="What ValidSim stores, what it logs, and what it does not collect."
>
  <Masthead slot="chrome" />

  <main id="main">
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="band-head">
          <p class="fig-label">Fig 0.6 — privacy</p>
          <h1 style="font-size: var(--t-hero); letter-spacing: -0.035em; max-width: 18ch;">
            What we store, and what we do not
          </h1>
          <p>
            ValidSim handles API keys, so this page is specific rather than generic. If something
            here is unclear or looks wrong, <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>ask us</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc">
          <h2>This website</h2>
          <p>
            This site is a static build. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics, embeds no third-party
            scripts, and has no advertising or tracking pixels. The only network request the page
            makes is for two webfonts, which is why we disclose it here.
          </p>

          <h2>The product</h2>
          <p>
            When you run ValidSim, the data stays where you run it. A local run uses an in-memory
            store that is discarded when the process exits; set a durable backend and the scorecards
            persist there. The API authenticates with an <code>X-API-Key</code> header compared in
            constant time. Keys are never logged, never written to a scorecard, and never included
            in an export.
          </p>

          <h2>Logs</h2>
          <p>
            The API emits structured JSON logs for operational debugging. Every request is logged with
            a method, path, status and duration. Request bodies, validation results and API keys are
            not logged. Logs are intended for a self-hosted deployment's own infrastructure.
          </p>

          <h2>What we collect from you</h2>
          <p>
            Nothing, unless you email us. This site has no form and no third-party embed, so there is
            no mechanism by which visiting it could identify you to us.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions, corrections, or a deletion request: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .doc h2 {
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-block-start: 2rem;
  }
  .doc p {
    color: var(--ink-mid);
  }
  .doc a {
    color: var(--unmeasured);
  }
  .doc code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
